# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT OR Apache-2.0
# Counterfactual: a sixth vocabulary rule admitting an unratified appointment-control source
#
# The ratified state-form sentence names five source kinds. One added line names
# a sixth — an incumbent-coalition affiliate — and it holds membership the moment
# anyone observes it. This is the shape the repository guard watches, because the
# assertion surface reconciles relations rather than heads and would not see it.
#
# What this fixture deliberately does NOT show is a finding passing on the new
# kind. The anti-capture rule names its five constants literally rather than
# through a variable, so a sixth member changes nothing a query can reach; the
# harm here is that a legal category widened by one source edit. Saying that
# plainly is the point of the fixture, and `src/checks/repository.rs` is what
# refuses it.
:expect-pins 2

observe(AppointmentWidenSource, AppointmentWidenRecord, IncumbentCoalitionAffiliateAppointmentSource, AppointmentControlSourceKindScope).

# The vocabulary grew: an unratified kind now holds membership.
? member(IncumbentCoalitionAffiliateAppointmentSource, AppointmentControlSourceKindVocabulary).
# => TRUE
# The control that keeps the line above from being vacuous: membership still
# requires its own ground rule, so an unobserved token holds nothing.
? member(ProfessionAppointmentSource, AppointmentControlSourceKindVocabulary).
# => FALSE
